	<b>News Archive</b><br><br>
	
	Jump to year: <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1104480000&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">2004</a> <br>Jump to month: <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1099206000&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">10/2004</a> <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1096527600&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">09/2004</a> <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1093935600&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">08/2004</a> <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1091257200&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">07/2004</a> <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1088578800&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">06/2004</a> <a href="newsarchive.php?start=1085986800&amp;PHPSESSID=3eaa8d34d23c93f71b3678d916d54cb8">05/2004</a> <br><br>	
				<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Tag, your IT!
					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Fri, May 21, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Welcome, one and all, to the Guardians of the Throne web page, where we have been forming a guild for almost a month now. however, in the past week or so, membership has really picked up. At the time of this post, we had 24 members, not accounts, but the people behind them.<br />
<br />
Some of you are aware the troubles this guild has been through since the beginning, but most of you do not. it took 2-3 weeks for our guild to be approved, but it is finally done, thanks to Mossy's perserverance. By now, most of you know two of the emails that she sent to EQGuilds to try to get our guild approved. She has promised to email copies of these so that I can then post them on the guild website.<br />
<br />
However, there is still one final obstacle in our way. None of us, including our fearless leader, the Princess, has a guild title.  TMS is petitioning to get her title, so that she, as leader, can invite us all into the guild. When I know more on the status of that, I shall inform you all.<br />
<br />
On a side note, I will be adding a few new forums, much like SOE did, to help distinguish between what content goes where. The first to go up will be an Off Topic board, for those things that we wish for only the guild to see. I will also put up class boards. Please, no ranting or flaming on these boards. These are not to say why a class is broken, or how SOE could better balance the classes, its for the people in the guild to ask questions for tips for their characters. As far as I know, SOE has no access to any of the boards, unless some of you in the guild work for SOE. After that, I may or may not build more boards. It depends on what people want.<br />
<br />
Also, I am going to experiment with grouping the boards, so it should be interesting, but I can't guarantee that it will work.<br />
<br />
I  update this message periodically, so remember to check back every once in a while.<br />
<br />
Questions? Comments? Concerns? I can always be reached at <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>. I just began checking my email every day. You can also use the EQ Message boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.
					<p>-- Coar
</p>
			</td></tr>
			</table><br />	
					<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Pictures, avitars, and the new webmaster!
					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Tue, May 11, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Ok, all, its time again. Time for what, you ask? Why, time for the newest bit of news from the newsdesk. As I get it, you get it. Currently, I have nothing new for you all in terms of the status of the guild creation. As far as I know, we are still waiting on GM contact in response to Lakotah's email.<br />
<br />
With the addition of the newest rank to SOE's message boards, the members now have the option of using personal avitars. If you cannot find one on the internet that you like, I am providing the extra option of uploading one from your computer. I am going to make a separate webpage to store these images, so they are protected. The following instructions should be used for any and all guild images sent to me for uploading.<br />
<br />
1. Give the picture what ever title you want for it, no spaces.<br />
2. Email me the picture. My email address is <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>.<br />
3. The subject of the email should include "Guild Image" and your SOE chat handle.<br />
4. Include a brief description of the picture/what it is for.<br />
5. I will upload the picture to the storage website.<br />
6. I will email you the details as to the address of your image, so you can use it else where.<br />
<br />
Unless you request otherwise, I will automatically add the picture to the images file cabinets, so that others can see them.<br />
<br />
Questions? Comments? Concerns? I can always be reached at <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>. I just began checking my email every day. You can also use the EQ Message boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.					<p>-- Coar
</p>
			</td></tr>
			</table><br />	
					<table class="tborder" width="99%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="4" border="0">
			<tr><td class="titlebg">
				<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%">
				<tr><td>
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Welcome to our new website!					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Sat, May 08, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Even though we are still trying to get on our feet, we finally have the guild name submitted for approval. As to the status of that, you will have to contact Lakotah, for she was made the guild leader, and as such, we must all wait on the Princess to receive more information from SOE as to the creation of the guild. Hopefully, that will be completed soon, and we will let you all know that it has begun, and the recruiting will start. For those of you who are interested in role-playing and are uncertain that this would be a good environment for you, there are plenty of you that are interested in the new guild, and you all will be treated with the same respect that everyone is treated.  I normally go back and forth between true role-play and non-role-play when I play, just based on how I feel at the time.<br />
<br />
Not much has been determined in terms of the roles of the members, like if we have a guild bank, who is running it, who will be in charge of planning raids (yes, even as newbies, we can raid, just small things, like Vex Thal, Plane of Time, and the Sleeper's Tomb, nothing big like Kurn's tower or Orc 1 in East Commonlands), or any other real details, I guess those will be determined at a later time.<br />
<br />
Questions? Comments? Concerns? I can always be reached at <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>. It may take a while for me to respond, because I don't check my email every day, but I will respond. You can also use the EQ Message boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.					<p>-- Coar
</p>
			</td></tr>
			</table><br />	
			
			<br /><br />
		</td></tr>
